@item CLI: @command{emacsctl tool mailbox agent-drop}
@item Surfaces: mcp, menu, agents
@item Returns: string
@item Flags: destructive
@end itemize

@multitable @columnfractions .2 .12 .1 .58
@headitem Argument @tab Type @tab Required @tab Description
@item @code{id} @tab string @tab yes @tab Task id, from agent_spawn
@item @code{index} @tab integer @tab no @tab Which queued message, from agent_inbox. Omit to clear the whole queue.
@end multitable

@item agent_inbox
List the messages queued for an agent that it has not yet been given. Use it to check whether something you sent has been picked up.

@itemize @bullet
@item CLI: @command{emacsctl tool mailbox agent-inbox}
@item Surfaces: mcp, dbus, cli, menu, agents
@item Returns: string
@end itemize

@multitable @columnfractions .2 .12 .1 .58
@headitem Argument @tab Type @tab Required @tab Description
@item @code{id} @tab string @tab yes @tab Task id, from agent_spawn
@end multitable

@item agent_log
Read the full transaction log of any agent -- every message it was given, every reply, every tool it called, in order. You do NOT need to have spawned it. This is how you inspect an agent that is misbehaving: read its log and see what it actually did, rather than what it says it did. Use from_turn to read only what is new since you last looked.

@itemize @bullet
@item CLI: @command{emacsctl tool mailbox agent-log}
@item Surfaces: mcp, dbus, cli, menu, agents
@item Returns: string
@end itemize

@multitable @columnfractions .2 .12 .1 .58
@headitem Argument @tab Type @tab Required @tab Description
@item @code{id} @tab string @tab yes @tab Task id of the agent to inspect
@item @code{from_turn} @tab integer @tab no @tab Only entries from this turn onward. Omit for all.
@item @code{kinds} @tab string @tab no @tab Comma-separated entry kinds to keep: message, reply, tool, state. Omit for all.
@end multitable

@item agent_send
Say something more to an agent. Works whether it is still running -- the message reaches it during its current turn when it can take one mid-turn, and otherwise when that turn ends -- or already finished, in which case it starts again with the same conversation and remembers everything from before. Returns immediately; poll with agent_status and collect with agent_result as usual.

@itemize @bullet
@item CLI: @command{emacsctl tool mailbox agent-send}
@item Surfaces: mcp, menu, agents
@item Returns: string
@item Flags: destructive, confirm=ask
@end itemize

@multitable @columnfractions .2 .12 .1 .58
@headitem Argument @tab Type @tab Required @tab Description
@item @code{id} @tab string @tab yes @tab Task id, from agent_spawn
@item @code{message} @tab string @tab yes @tab What to say. It continues the existing conversation, so you do not need to repeat context you already gave it.
@end multitable

@end table

