@subheading web

@table @code
@item web_lql
Run an LQL query on the libresearch metasearch server and return the rows. LQL is a pipeline over search results, e.g. `search "glib", category: CODE | filter extra.stars > 100 | fields title, url' or the shorthand `gtk docs | filter site("docs.gtk.org")'. With explain, return the plan without running it. Use web_research instead for a plain question.

@itemize @bullet
@item CLI: @command{emacsctl tool web lql}
@item Surfaces: mcp, dbus, cli, menu, agents
@item Returns: string
@end itemize

@multitable @columnfractions .2 .12 .1 .58
@headitem Argument @tab Type @tab Required @tab Description
@item @code{query} @tab string @tab yes @tab The LQL query
@item @code{explain} @tab boolean @tab no @tab Plan the query without running it
@end multitable

@item web_research
Research a question on the web and return a cited answer. A libresearch server searches, reads the most relevant pages and answers with numbered citations [n], followed by the sources it cites (title and URL). Use it for questions that need current or external facts; cite the sources you rely on. Slow: a run takes one to several minutes, longer with deep.

@itemize @bullet
@item CLI: @command{emacsctl tool web research}
@item Surfaces: mcp, dbus, cli, menu, agents
@item Returns: string
@end itemize

@multitable @columnfractions .2 .12 .1 .58
@headitem Argument @tab Type @tab Required @tab Description
@item @code{question} @tab string @tab yes @tab The question to answer, as a full sentence
@item @code{deep} @tab boolean @tab no @tab Let the server run follow-up searches (slower, more thorough)
@item @code{pages} @tab integer @tab no @tab Pages to read, 1-20; omit for the server's default
@end multitable

@item web_search_show
Open a libresearch web search in a results grid in the user's editor, for the USER to read, sort, mark and act on. Returns at once; it does not return the results to you (use web_research or web_lql for that). Use it when the user asks to see or browse search results.

@itemize @bullet
@item CLI: @command{emacsctl tool web search-show}
@item Surfaces: mcp, dbus, cli, menu, agents
@item Returns: string
@end itemize

@multitable @columnfractions .2 .12 .1 .58
@headitem Argument @tab Type @tab Required @tab Description
@item @code{query} @tab string @tab yes @tab What to search for
@item @code{category} @tab string @tab no @tab A category: general, news, code, science, it, ...
@end multitable

@end table

@subheading window

@table @code
@item current_view
What the user is looking at right now: the visible buffers, most recently selected first, with the AI chat surfaces excluded. Call this when the user refers to "here", "this" or "the above" without naming a buffer.

